          "passage": "Tanya Tagaq is a writer and musician and a\nmember of the Inuit community of Cambridge\nBay in northern Canada. Critics and fellow\nwriters have praised her work for combining\ntraditional Inuit stories with popular genres of\nliterature, such as fantasy fiction. But Tagaq is\nnot the only Indigenous writer to blend\ntraditional stories with popular literature. In\nthe 2020 novel The Only Good Indians, Stephen\nGraham Jones successfully blended the oral\nstorytelling tradition of his tribe, the Blackfeet\nNation, with horror fiction.",
