          "passageTitle": "Main Ideas — Q38",
          "passage": "Mauricio Drelichman and Hans-Joachim Voth's\nresearch into the debt defaults of Philip II (who\nruled an empire including Spain and much of\nBelgium from 1556 to 1598) relates to other\nwork on European early modern state finance,\nincluding Hoffman and Norberg's research on\nthe relationship between state finance and\npolitical development. But Drelichman and\nVoth's unique contribution to the field is their\nreconstruction of the earliest extant set of\nannual fiscal records for any sovereign state,\ndemonstrating in turn that Philip's defaults\nwere caused by short-term cash shortages, not\nlong-term unsustainable debts.",
